  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner), according to Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner), according to Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner), the EPA waiver allows California to limit the number of vehicles that run on liquid fuel; vacating the waiver would redress the petitioners\u2019 injuries because they make and sell liquid fuel."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner), according to Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner), according to Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner), when the government denies a party the ability to compete in a marketplace, the party\u2019s claim for market\u2011restriction relief is redressable because the party is asking for the injurious restriction to be removed."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 68,
                "start": 68
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Jeffrey B. Wall, because the market\u2019s future trajectory is uncertain, the petitioners argue that they should be allowed to compete now rather than wait for speculative predictions."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b5d7daa366245deda468df4b5f19d0cc00a08aeeada5d83c308abad031571c2a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b5d7daa36624-0002-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argued, relying on statements from California regulators and the EPA, that the shift toward fuel efficiency would reduce demand for fossil fuels, causing a financial injury."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners (Diamond Alternative Energy and others)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "EPA",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b5d7daa366245deda468df4b5f19d0cc00a08aeeada5d83c308abad031571c2a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b5d7daa36624-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 15,
                "start": 15
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The EPA argued that the fuel producers did not establish redressability because they failed to show that invalidating the California regulations would cause automakers to produce fewer electric vehicles and more gasoline\u2011powered vehicles."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "State Respondents",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to State Respondents, state respondents asserted that federal courts presume lack of standing and that petitioners must prove each element of standing."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "State Respondents",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "State respondents argued that petitioners failed to show a non\u2011speculative likelihood that automakers would sell more gasoline cars if the waiver were vacated."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "California",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b5d7daa366245deda468df4b5f19d0cc00a08aeeada5d83c308abad031571c2a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b5d7daa36624-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 2,
                "start": 2
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "California argued that the fuel producers lacked standing because automobile manufacturers would not change their production in response to a vacated waiver, given the surge in consumer demand for electric vehicles."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondents (Environmental Protection Agency and others)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
